    "evidence_text": "Outcome of multipair donor kidney exchange by a web-based algorithm.\n\nFifty-three DRP were enrolled from five transplant centers.\n\nKidney paired donation and optimizing the use of live donor organs.\n\nDespite its increasing popularity, very few transplants have resulted from KPD.   \n\n\nEven if only 7% of patients awaiting kidney transplantation participated in an optimized national KPD program, the health care system could save as much as $750 million.   \n\n\nManaging finances of shipping living donor kidneys for donor exchanges.\n\nBilling between hospitals is based on Medicare cost report defined costs rather than charges.\n\nSystemic arterial hypertension in children following renal transplantation: prevalence and risk factors.\n\nyes versus no).\n\nSuccessful three-way kidney paired donation with cross-country live donor allograft transport.\n\nIncidence of skin cancer after renal transplantation in The Netherlands.\n\nWe assessed the effects of these drug combinations on progression of chronic kidney disease.   \n\n\nAnalysis was by intention to treat (ITT).\n\nFUNDING Novartis.\n\nCall to Develop a Standard Acquisition Charge Model for Kidney Paired Donation\n\nWe propose a Medicare Demonstration Project to develop a standard acquisition charge for kidney paired donation.\n\nLiver transplantation and opioid dependence.\n\nNinety-four percent have addiction treatment requirements.",
